11. MANUAL PAYMENT SYSTEM
Manual payment is the approved payment arrangement for the current development stage.
AIDOMART must allow sellers to provide their own accurate payment details and allow buyers to make payments directly using the relevant seller's instructions.
There must be no payment gateway, automatic money transfer, automatic payment splitting or automated payment processing.
11.1 Seller payment settings
Each seller must have a Payment Settings area in their dashboard.
The seller should be able to configure their accepted manual payment methods.
Mobile Money details may include:
Provider, such as MTN Mobile Money, Telecel Cash or AT Money, where applicable.
Registered account holder's full name.
Mobile Money number.
Payment instructions.
Bank-transfer details may include:
Bank name.
Full registered account holder's name.
Account number.
Branch and other relevant details.
The seller must be able to update their payment details.
The system must display the actual saved information accurately.
11.2 Unique order reference
Every order must receive a unique reference generated automatically by the system.
The reference must:
Be generated on the server.
Be unique in the database.
Be associated with the correct order.
Be visible to the buyer and relevant seller.
Appear on the order confirmation and payment instructions.
The buyer must be instructed to include the unique order reference in the payment narration or reference field wherever supported.
11.3 Buyer payment instructions
The buyer must see:
Order reference.
Relevant seller.
Products covered by the payment.
Exact amount payable.
Available payment method.
Correct recipient name.
Correct account or wallet number.
Clear payment instructions.
Only payment methods configured by the seller should be displayed.
11.4 I Have Made Payment
The order details page must provide an I Have Made Payment button.
When the buyer selects it, the system should allow them to report:
Payment method used.
Amount reportedly paid.
Transaction reference or ID, where available.
Date and time, where available.
Relevant additional information.
The system must save the report and set the status to:
Payment Reported — Awaiting Seller Verification
This must not automatically confirm payment.
11.5 Seller payment verification
The seller must have a Payment Verification area in their dashboard.
The seller must manually check the actual receiving Mobile Money or bank account before confirming receipt.
The seller should be able to:
Confirm payment received.
Report payment not received.
Flag an incorrect amount.
Flag an unmatched transaction.
Flag a suspicious report.
Request additional information.
A buyer's screenshot, receipt, transaction code or statement must not automatically be treated as proof that payment was received.
When the seller confirms payment, the system must record the seller responsible, date, time, relevant order and amount confirmed.
11.6 Payment statuses
Payment status must remain separate from order status.
Relevant payment statuses include:
Not Reported.
Payment Reported — Awaiting Seller Verification.
Payment Confirmed.
Payment Not Received.
Payment Amount Mismatch.
Payment Under Review.
Payment Cancelled.
Refund Pending.
Refunded.
A payment must only be marked confirmed after the required manual verification.
A refund must only be marked completed after the refund has actually taken place.
11.7 Multi-seller payments
Where an order involves products from different sellers, the system must distinguish each seller's payable amount and payment details.
Each seller must verify only payments associated with their own orders.
If the existing architecture cannot safely support this arrangement, the developer must implement an appropriate seller-specific order process rather than creating an unreliable combined-payment process.
There must be no automatic splitting or transfer of money between sellers.
11.8 Payment records
The system must retain relevant payment records, including:
Order reference.
Seller and buyer associations.
Amount due.
Amount reported.
Amount confirmed.
Payment method.
Transaction reference, where available.
Payment status.
Reporting date and time.
Verification date and time.
User responsible for important actions.
Relevant verification notes and history.
Buyers, sellers and administrators must only access payment information they are authorised to see.
