13. PROMOTIONAL CODES AND DISCOUNTS
The project owner has requested dashboard-based promotional functionality involving promo codes and percentage discounts.
The intended functionality includes:
Creating promotional codes.
Setting the discount percentage.
Applying the correct discount calculation.
Setting a start date and expiry date.
Viewing active and expired promotions.
Ending a promotion.
Extending a promotion by changing its expiry date.
Ensuring a promotion automatically expires when its end date is reached.
The system must calculate discounts correctly and display the correct discounted amount.
Promotional codes must be validated by the backend before they are applied to an order. The frontend must not be trusted to calculate or authorise discounts by itself.
The system must check the promotion's validity dates and other configured conditions before accepting a code.
Once the expiry date and time are reached, the promotion must automatically become inactive and must no longer be accepted at checkout.
Extending a promotion must update its expiry date correctly and retain the appropriate record of the change.
Important clarification for implementation: The request refers to buyers creating promotions in their dashboards. The developer must not silently change this to seller-created promotions. The project owner must confirm whether promo-code creation is intended for buyers, sellers, or both before the permission rules and dashboard interface are finalised.
