17. SECURITY AND PROTECTION AGAINST ATTACKS
Security is a major requirement of AIDOMART.
The website must be developed with appropriate protection against common web application attacks, unauthorised access, account compromise and misuse of marketplace functionality.
The developer must implement and test appropriate protections, including:
Secure password hashing.
Secure authentication and session management.
Server-side input validation.
Protection against SQL injection.
Protection against cross-site scripting (XSS).
Cross-site request forgery (CSRF) protection.
Secure file-upload validation and storage.
Access control and role-based permissions.
Rate limiting for sensitive actions such as login, registration and verification.
Protection against unauthorised changes to prices, discounts, orders and payment statuses.
Secure handling of email verification and password-reset tokens.
Secure storage of API keys and other secrets.
Protection of private seller documents and buyer information.
Appropriate error handling without exposing internal technical details.
HTTPS in the deployed production environment.
All permissions must be enforced on the server, not merely by hiding buttons or pages in the interface.
A buyer must not be able to access another buyer's private information.
A seller must not be able to access another seller's private products, orders or payment records.
An ordinary buyer or seller must not be able to access administrative functions.
The developer must not claim that the website is completely immune to attacks. Security must be assessed through appropriate testing and maintained as the project develops.
